# Receipts are evidence, not source.
#
# Every file under receipts/ was written on the build machine, in LF, and the
# reports print sha256 sums OF THOSE BYTES: BUILD-20260831T123738Z.md tells a
# reader that receipts.jsonl hashes to 9d30878d…, and invites them to check.
# With git's usual text handling a Windows checkout hands that reader a CRLF
# copy hashing to f9ad7062…, and the receipt's own instruction fails in their
# hands — for a reason that has nothing to do with the build.
#
# -text: no conversion in either direction. What was committed is what lands
# on disk, on every platform, so a printed hash is checkable where it is read.
receipts/** -text
